{"id":"healthlake","corpus":"aws","title":"AWS HealthLake","sourceUrl":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/healthlake/latest/devguide/what-is.html","license":"AWS Documentation © Amazon Web Services, Inc.","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"AWS HealthLake"},{"kind":"p","text":"AWS HealthLake is a HIPAA eligible service for storing, analyzing, and sharing health data in the cloud using the Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources (FHIR) R4 specification. HealthLake use cases include:"},{"kind":"li","text":"Enterprise health data – Manage and share FHIR R4 health data directly from AWS Cloud while preserving high performance and availability."},{"kind":"li","text":"Healthcare interoperability – Support customer conformance with 21st Century Cures Act for patient access through a fully managed FHIR data store."},{"kind":"li","text":"Healthcare data transformation – Convert legacy C-CDA and CSV data into FHIR R4 with the data transformation AI agent without building or maintaining conversion pipelines."},{"kind":"li","text":"Natural language processing (NLP) – Utilize integrated NLP models to extract meaningful medical information from unstructured health data."},{"kind":"li","text":"Multimodal analysis – Combine HealthLake data with AWS HealthImaging data and AWS HealthOmics data to deliver insights for precision medicine."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Important notice"},{"kind":"p","text":"AWS HealthLake is not a substitute for professional medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment, and is not intended to cure, treat, mitigate, prevent, or diagnose any disease or health condition. You are responsible for instituting human review as part of any use of AWS HealthLake, including in association with any third-party product intended to inform clinical decision-making. AWS HealthLake should only be used in patient care or clinical scenarios after review by trained medical professionals applying sound medical judgment."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Features of AWS HealthLake"},{"kind":"p","text":"AWS HealthLake provides the following features."},{"kind":"p","text":"Convert legacy healthcare data to FHIR R4 with the Data Transformation Agent (Preview)"},{"kind":"p","text":"With HealthLake's Data Transformation Agent, you can convert legacy healthcare data into the FHIR R4 standard without any FHIR expertise. You start from a working profile: for C-CDA, the AWS Starter Profile provides common section-to-resource mappings out of the box; for relational data, the agent generates a base profile tailored to your schema from sample CSVs. Use a profile as-is, or refine it as needed with the AI agent."},{"kind":"p","text":"Import FHIR R4 health data"},{"kind":"p","text":"With the HealthLake native import action, you can easily migrate your FHIR data from an Amazon S3 bucket to an HealthLake data store, including clinical notes, lab reports, insurance claims, and more. HealthLake supports the FHIR R4 specification for health care data exchange. If your data isn't already in FHIR R4, use the Data Transformation Agent to convert C-CDA and CSV data yourself, or work with an AWS HealthLake Partner."},{"kind":"p","text":"Store health data in a secure, compliant, and auditable manner"},{"kind":"p","text":"A HealthLake data store helps index health data so it can be queried. The data store creates a complete view of each patient’s medical history in chronological order and facilitates information exchange using the FHIR R4 specification. And it's always running to keep your index up to date, offering you the ability to search the information anytime using standard FHIR R4 interactions with durable primary storage and index scaling. HealthLake also automatically detects and links duplicate records (Preview), so each patient or entity is represented once across sources."},{"kind":"p","text":"Leverage transactional FHIR server"},{"kind":"p","text":"Leverage FHIR APIs for standard resource validation, SMART on FHIR authorization, and Bulk data FHIR API export capabilities to support unifying and analyzing your data to reduce operational costs and improve decision making. HealthLake supports customer conformity to the latest ONC and CMS regulatory standards including: HL7 FHIR R4 APIs, FHIR Bulk Data Access, US Core IG STU, HL7 SMART App Launch Framework IG, OAuth 2.0, and OpenID Connect."},{"kind":"p","text":"Transform unstructured medical data using NLP"},{"kind":"p","text":"Integrated medical natural language processing (NLP) transforms all raw medical text data in a HealthLake data store to understand and extract meaningful information from unstructured healthcare data. With integrated medical NLP, you can automatically extract entities, entity relationships, entity traits, and protected health information (PHI) from your medical text. The NLP-extracted entities are stored as native FHIR R4 resources within a HealthLake data store and can be accessed through FHIR R4 APIs or Amazon Athena (SQL)."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Related AWS services"},{"kind":"p","text":"AWS HealthLake features tight integration with other AWS services. A knowledge of the following services is useful to fully leverage HealthLake."},{"kind":"li","text":"AWS Identity and Access Management – Use IAM to securely manage identities and access to HealthLake resources."},{"kind":"li","text":"Amazon Simple Storage Service – Use Amazon S3 as a staging area to import DICOM data into HealthLake."},{"kind":"li","text":"AWS CloudTrail – Use CloudTrail to track HealthLake user activity and API usage."}],"lemmas":{"eligibles":["eligibles","eligible"],"serviced":["serviced","service"],"servicing":["servicing","service"],"storing":["storing","store"],"storings":["storings","storing"],"stores":["store","stores"],"analyzing":["analyzing","analyze"],"analyzings":["analyzings","analyzing"],"analyzes":["analyzes","analyze"],"analyzed":["analyzed","analyze"],"sharing":["sharing","share"],"sharings":["sharing","sharings"],"shares":["share","shares"],"shared":["shared","share"],"data":["datum